From a8c37573d9075c0b3ed8c1b8eb92692a54a42add Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: eileenthg <40307498+eileenthg@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 6 Sep 2026 00:40:04 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Add goat cheese as a third cheese type

Migrates Expanded Delight's goat cheese into B&C as a full cheese type
alongside Flaxen and Scarlet, using B&C's existing keg pipeline rather
than ED's cask mechanic.

ED's plain "Cheese" is deliberately NOT ported: it is functionally the
same as Flaxen Cheese, so bringing it across would recreate the overlap
this migration exists to remove. Only goat cheese is genuinely new.

Pipeline mirrors the existing cheeses end to end:
  goat milk -> ferment (honeycomb, wheat seeds, sugar, rennet @ temp 4)
  -> goat cheese fluid -> pour with honeycomb -> unripe wheel -> ages
  -> ripe wheel -> knife-cut into 8 wedges -> 8 wedges craft back

Adds two fluids (goat_cheese, goat_milk) across common and both loader
implementations, the wheel/unripe-wheel blocks, the wedge and its food
properties, fluid/item/block tags, loot and the slicing loot modifier,
an advancement criterion, and JEI + EMI entries.

Goat milk is intentionally not implemented here. A NeoForge-only pouring
recipe, gated on neoforge:mod_loaded expandeddelight, fills the goat milk
fluid from ED's goat milk bucket. Consequence: goat cheese is unobtainable
in a B&C-only install.

Textures are derived from the flaxen set by a hue/saturation shift to a
pale ivory, and are placeholder quality pending real art.

Also fixes a pre-existing typo in BnCFluidTags: the scarlet_cheese fluid
tag contained FLOWING_FLAXEN_CHEESE instead of FLOWING_SCARLET_CHEESE.

Verified: :neoforge:compileJava, :fabric:compileJava, and :neoforge:runData
all pass. Not yet tested in game.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
